[[File:Cyclooctadiene-rhodium-chloride-dimer-2D-skeletal.png|thumb|Cyclooctadiene rhodium chloride dimer]]'''Organorhodium chemistry''' is the [[chemistry]] of [[organometallic compounds]] containing a [[rhodium]]-[[carbon]] [[chemical bond]], and the study of rhodium and rhodium compounds as [[catalyst]]s in [[organic reaction]]s.<ref>''Synthesis of Organometallic Compounds: A Practical Guide'' Sanshiro Komiya Ed. S. Komiya, M. Hurano 1997</ref>

