The '''Institute for Astronomy and Astrophysics''' ('''IAA''') in [[Brussels]] is a part of the physics department of the [[Université Libre de Bruxelles]]. It is an international center of excellence in the field of [[nuclear astrophysics]]. The institute's director is currently Prof. Alain Jorissen. The institute is composed of one full professor, five tenured [[NFWO|FNRS]] senior researchers, nine postdoctoral fellows from various countries ([[Belgium]], [[France]], [[Japan]], [[United Kingdom]], [[Slovakia]]), and three Ph.D. students (Belgium, [[Italy]]).
